pub const CHAPTER_5_PLAIN_SYSTEM_INSTRUCTION: &str = "Design Considerations and Strategies\n\nThis chapter focuses on the design constraints, architectural strategies, and cost-benefit analysis of the project. It aims to provide a detailed, well-structured approach to these critical elements.\n\n## **Design Constraints**\n\n**Hardware and Software Environment**\n\n- **Hardware Requirements:**\n - Specify necessary computer specifications, including CPU, RAM, and storage.\n - Identify additional peripherals and confirm network requirements.\n- **Software Requirements:**\n - List required operating systems with version compatibility.\n - Identify necessary libraries and frameworks with specified versions and dependencies.\n- **Cloud and Virtualization:**\n - Assess the need for cloud services or virtualization like virtual machines or containers.\n - Identify potential hosting service providers.\n- **Software Licensing and Costs:**\n - Research software licensing requirements and calculate associated costs.\n- **Environment Configuration:**\n - Create a detailed setup guide with troubleshooting resources.\n- **Review and Update:**\n - Regularly review and update hardware and software requirements as the project progresses.\n\n**End-User Characteristics**\n\n- **Target User Demographic:**\n - Identify age, geographic location, and education level.\n- **Technical Skills:**\n - Assess familiarity with technology and commonly used devices.\n- **Knowledge Base:**\n - Determine subject matter expertise and industry knowledge.\n- **Specific Needs and Limitations:**\n - Address accessibility requirements, language preferences, and customization needs.\n- **User Feedback:**\n - Conduct surveys or interviews to gather direct feedback and compile findings into a user profile report.\n\n## **Architectural Strategies**\n\n**Used Algorithms**\n\n- **Scope and Objectives:**\n - Define the project's goals and criteria for choosing algorithms.\n- **Research and Evaluation:**\n - Analyze potential algorithms for efficiency, scalability, accuracy, and select the best fit.\n- **Implementation and Documentation:**\n - Document the chosen algorithms, their roles in achieving project objectives, and the reasons for selection.\n- **Review and Optimization:**\n - Continually refine algorithm performance based on testing results.\n\n**Reuse of Existing Software Components**\n\n- **Identification:**\n - Identify third-party libraries, frameworks, or components used.\n- **Description and Purpose:**\n - Describe each component's purpose and how it enhances project development.\n- **Benefits Analysis:**\n - Evaluate improvements in development efficiency, performance, and community support.\n- **Documentation:**\n - Provide comprehensive documentation, including licensing information.\n\n## **Project Management**\n\n**Management Strategies**\n\n- Discuss the methodologies used, such as Agile or Waterfall, and their application principles.\n\n**Tasks and Resources**\n\n- Enumerate major project tasks with descriptions, resources needed, and potential risks.\n\n**Development Method**\n\n- Explain the software development methodology, detailing phases and tools used.\n\n**Future Enhancement Plans**\n\n- Outline potential future improvements and their feasibility.\n\n**System Architecture Diagram**\n\n- Create an Archimate diagram using PlantUML code to depict the system architecture according to specifications.\n\n## **Costs and Benefits**\n\n**Cost Analysis**\n\n- Examine projected costs for development, hardware, software, and maintenance.\n\n**Benefit Analysis**\n\n- Assess potential technical achievements and broader impacts like efficiency improvements and societal contributions.\n\n**Cost-Benefit Comparison**\n\n- Compare costs versus benefits to evaluate the project's overall value and feasibility.\n\nThis structured approach ensures clarity and comprehensive coverage of critical project aspects, employing suitable technical terminology and maintaining originality.\n";
